  "- Stk1 and Stp1 have dark centres and fixed central positions. This emphasizes their biological role; it is not a claim of data-derived centrality or distance.",
  "- All isolates are packed with their annotation/context region, rather than on a distant bottom row. Canvas dimensions follow occupied content.",
  "- The three effect rings keep a common +/-2 scale. The compact footer combines ring order, effect legend and outline key.",
  "- Pathway outlines use distinct blue, orange, charcoal and magenta/purple hues, supplemented with solid/dashed/dot-dash/dotted styles, explicit pathway names and P/R/N/T membership badges. Colour is not the only way to distinguish groups; node centres are neutral.",
  "- Every node appears once. Membership data and plotting code support multiple badges/overlapping regions when required. There are no actual shared memberships across these four terms in either current input set; no overlap was invented.",
  "- PNG files are300dpi. PDF/SVG retain vector elements for poster enlargement. Original step6 network figures remain unchanged in their previous folder.","",
  "## Current STRING memberships differ from the course scope","",
