md <- c(md,"",
  "All discrepancies are course-only purine assignments; the other three pathway memberships agree exactly. Proteins outside these four fresh assignments remain visible as additional selected context proteins. Missing current membership is not proof of an incorrect course annotation or an unimportant protein; accessory roles and reference/version differences can contribute. The historical ORA/GSEA sets, NES and FDRs have not been changed or retested.","",
  "Current annotation-region colours are not Leiden communities. The native STRING reference images are also archived: those reproduce an evidence-edge display with Leiden resolution0.7 and no added nodes. Leiden resolution0.7 is separate from interaction confidence0.4. Custom poster placement/outlines intentionally show annotation groups instead of pretending to reproduce Leiden clustering.","",
  "[Course versus live membership by protein](course_vs_live_KEGG_membership.csv) · [Current memberships](pathway_membership_live.csv) · [Exact-list comparison](input_set_comparison.csv).","",
  "## Read the rings","",
  "| Position | Interaction effect | Positive means |","|---|---|---|",
  "| Inner | stk/anc = R_anc - R_stk | SN response is more positive in anc than stk |",
  "| Middle | stp/anc = R_anc - R_stp | SN response is more positive in anc than stp |",
  "| Outer | stp/stk = R_stk - R_stp | SN response is more positive in stk than stp |","",
  "R is the model SN-minus-TSB response. Blue is negative; white is zero; orange-red is positive. Grey means no suitable quantitative estimate, including source-LOD/other models or fewer than2/3 relevant detections; it is not a zero. Black dots show supplied protein FDR<0.1. Numeric estimates, source-model labels and detection counts remain in node CSVs. Display colours alone are clipped outside+/-2; data values are unchanged.","",
  "The three contrasts are algebraically dependent and are not independent replication. These are total-protein abundances, not phosphorylation or enzyme activity. STRING confidence represents support for an association, not interaction strength. Central placement and an edge do not establish direct binding or Stk1/Stp1 substrate relationships.","",
